text:
- Great location (15' walk to Time Square and major subway lines and 10' walk to cruise departure around Manhattan;
- Good quality/price if budget is an important factor: taxes already included in the price, breakfast included, which with NYC prices, is a nice plus; 
- Simple structure, rooms a little small, good cleaning with daily change of towels; Wi-Fi available and with good reception;
- Breakfast included; possibility to cook waffles, bagels with jam, egg, cheese, bananas, yogurt, cereals, milk and juices, coffee available 24 hours a day;
- Helpful and friendly staff, reception H24;

I stayed at this guesthouse (because this is what it is, not a hotel) in December 2024. What about...

Positive side:
- really great location to get around Rome even on foot! 

Negatives:
- impossibility to communicate with those who manage the structure;
- problems (invented by them) in the booking confirmation due to the invalidity of the credit card (not true, worked perfectly);
- no lift (with room on the fourth floor);
- hairdryer in the bathroom with broken safety grill. Consequence: inside the hairdryer the propeller sucked a whole lock of hair;
- cleaning to review. 

Average.
